scoring:
Read every 50 ms step from the poses and contacts of the chest, head, mask, bag, grippers and manikin. In a real trial: the phone's side video (the flag dot's rise is scaled by its own 10 mm diameter and taken from its height in the first second, before the start), the station videos, the tape marks and the Laerdal QCPR Learner app (a new session each trial; its ventilation count is read off the phone when the trial ends; if it and the video disagree, the video decides).
- Seated: the mask covers the nose and mouth, its narrow end on the bridge of the nose below the eyes and its wide end on the chin above its point (sim: mask centre within 6 mm of the point midway between them, all 12 cuff segments pressed 1 mm on the face).
- Breath: while the mask is seated and nothing touches the manikin but the mask and the gripper holding it on the head, the flag dot rises at least 5 mm above its resting height, peaks no more than 12 mm up, 0.5 s to 2 s after it starts to rise, then falls back within 2 mm of rest; in a real trial the app counts a ventilation for it.
- Too big: any seated, clean rise peaking more than 12 mm up, whatever its timing (about 8 mL/kg for the 6 kg infant).
- Held off: the mask 30 mm or more from the face, the bag-valve mask in a gripper and still for 1 s.
- 0 for the rest of the run if: the manikin moves 20 mm from its outline or its back lifts 5 mm off the mat; the mask's rim presses on an eye for 1 s or more; the bag-valve mask is dropped onto the manikin.
- Otherwise, at the end of the run:
  - 1.0: exactly two breaths, none too big, then held off;
  - 0.75: exactly two breaths, none too big, but the mask left on the face, not held still, or dropped or put down;
  - 0.5: one breath; or three or more; or any breath plus a too-big one;
  - 0.25: no breath, but the mask seated for 2 s or more;
  - 0: anything else.
Which hand holds the mask doesn't matter. The trial ends once 1.0 has held for 1 s, in a real trial too.
